# samples/03-CustomProcessors – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/03-CustomProcessors
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5103
@apiKey = sample-api-key

### Typed processor with a configuration
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/Ada

### One processor, two configurations
GET {{baseUrl}}/calc/sum?a=2&b=40

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/calc/average?values=1&values=2&values=6

### Inline processor
GET {{baseUrl}}/time?timeZone=Europe/Warsaw

### DI and database access – create a note
# @name note
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Buy milk", "content": "2 litres" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{note.response.body.id}}

### Filter: 401 without the API key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{note.response.body.id}}

### …204 with it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{note.response.body.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Filter on rejected requests: see the X-Validation-Errors header
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "x" }

### File upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=sample

--sample
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Contract
--sample
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="contract.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.7 not really a PDF, but the content type says so
--sample--

### Handing work on: the validator parses the CSV once
POST {{baseUrl}}/imports/csv
Content-Type: application/json

{ "csv": "sku,quantity\nANV-1,2\nROC-2,1" }

### …a wrong header
POST {{baseUrl}}/imports/csv
Content-Type: application/json

{ "csv": "name\nAda" }

### Custom management API: publish an endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/greetings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "pirate", "greeting": "Ahoy" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/greetings/pirate/Jack

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/greetings

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/greetings/pirate
